<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Campaign</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ten Days' Campaign</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1831</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgian-revolution">Belgian Revolution</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Ten Days' Campaign was the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> invasion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgium">Belgium</a> in August 1831, an attempt by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-i-of-the-netherlands">King William I of the Netherlands</a> to reverse the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgian-revolution">Belgian Revolution</a>. Dutch forces defeated the Belgian armies at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hasselt">Hasselt</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leuven">Leuven</a>, but withdrew when a French army entered Belgium to support the new state. The campaign left Belgian independence intact, although the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a> recognised it only in 1839.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ten-days-campaign.jpg" alt="Ten Days' Campaign" width="320" height="226" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unkown, but after a painting of Cornelis Kruseman · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_replacement_of_the_injured_horse_of_the_Prince_of_Orange_during_the_battle_of_Boutersem_in_1831_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
